es nothing.** In the Add medicine sheet, an injection with Preparation type \"Ampule\" selected can't be saved. Save gives no message and the sheet stays open. Vial saved fine.\n2. **Singular/plural on the card subtitle.** A dose of one tablet reads \"Oral · 1 tablets · 1 mg\". The fractional doses 1/2, 1/3 and 1/8 also use the plural (\"1/2 tablets\").\n\n**What I covered**\n- **Medicines list:** the headers (Estradiol, Antiandrogen) matched the items under them after each save.\n- **Category picker:** all five categories (Estradiol, Antiandrogen, SERM, GnRHa, Custom) showed the right forms and medications.\n- **Saving medicines:** Tablet, Vial injection, Patch and Antiandrogen tablet all saved and showed the correct subtitle. Saving a Patch also added a \"Remove patch\" medicine that I never created. I took that as intended and didn't report it.\n- **Dosing on cards:** I checked the card subtitle at 1/8, 1/3, 1/2 and 1 tablet per dose.\n\n**Not tested**\n- The Gel form's Container/Sachet save, which is likely to hit the same default-selected problem as Ampule.\n- The 1/4 dose step.\n- Screen rotation.\n- Leaving and coming back to check that edits were kept.\n\nI also noticed the 1/8 tablet dose shows \"0.13 mg\" for a 0.125 mg dose. That may just be rounding, so I didn't report it.\n\nConfidence in the sign-off was 0.6.", "ttft_ms": 1815, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 231670, "uuid": "74d45758-76ce-4975-bdda-89f134afdd5b", "ttft_stream_ms": 1293, "time_to_request_ms": 350, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 4, "system_prompt": 8, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 2, "input_attachments": 4, "input_hooks": 2, "conversation_append": 0, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "init_frame_send": 2, "engine_pickup": 0, "loop_entry": 2, "message_prep": 1, "model_config_wait": 0, "autocompact": 1, "request_announcements": 3, "query_setup": 1, "model_gates": 307, "tool_schema_build": 2, "message_normalization": 2, "client_creation": 1, "request_build": 4}